tps://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-06T05:29:29Z","updated_at":"2025-04-06T05:29:29Z","body":"There are still a few cases to figure out, and then the other tasks to complete as well, but I think this is close enough to complete now that it'd make sense to open it for review. I'm also keeping the commits separate for now (i.e., not squashing) since I'm trying to include one type of detection per commit so I can tell them apart easier. Once it's ready for merging, I'll squash and force push.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2781229393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783797358","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104955#issuecomment-2783797358","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104955","id":2783797358,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6l7WBu","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-07T15:39:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-07T15:39:10Z","body":"All of my test cases appear to be working now!\r\n\r\nI would really appreciate it if someone more familiar with the GDScript parser could take a look at `gdscript_analyzer.cpp:4033`. The current way I'm distinguishing native and user-defined enums feels a bit hacky, so if there's a better way to do it then I'd be all for it.\r\n\r\nI've also noticed that as a little quirk of the identifier recognition, accessing a deprecated property from within its getter or setter causes those lines to trigger the warning.\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2025-04-07 at 08 35 53@2x](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ac8a76c8-1677-42a3-9feb-a908533d9ebe)\r\n\r\nUltimately, it *does* make sense, I guess - you are using the deprecated identifier - but in this specific context, it's a bit funny for it to complain about.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2783797358/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2785197021","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104955#issuecomment-2785197021","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104955","id":2785197021,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mArvd","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T04:33:27Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T04:33:27Z","body":"Warnings now display information about what exactly is deprecated!\r\n\r\n![CleanShot 2025-04-07 at 21 30 58@2x](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/802146b7-f76e-48ba-8943-07d17e9e80f7)\r\n\r\nThe only case that doesn't seem to work right is when an autoload's global variable name is used as a type specifier:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar my_autoload: SomeAutoload\r\n```\r\nI'm having trouble extracting the name `SomeAutoload` to display in the warning. But I'm not entirely sure if that *should* be allowed. In any case, for right now it just defaults to \"The class is deprecated\".\r\n\r\nI tried regenerating the GDScript tests, but one of them is causing a hard crash. I'll have to look more at it over the next couple of days when I have time.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2785197021/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2786847578","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104955#issuecomment-2786847578","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104955","id":2786847578,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mG-ta","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T15:32:10Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T15:48:20Z","body":"I'm getting a crash while typing an enum name.\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node2D\r\n\r\nenum MyEnum {\r\n\tOPTION1,\r\n\tOPTION2\r\n}\r\n\r\n# Type MyEnum here to crash.\r\nvar my_enum:\r\n```\r\n\r\n> I would really appreciate it if someone more familiar with the GDScript parser could take a look at `gdscript_analyzer.cpp:4033`. The current way I'm distinguishing native and user-defined enums feels a bit hacky, so if there's a better way to do it then I'd be all for it.\r\n\r\nThere is `CoreConstants::is_global_enum(name)`.\r\n\r\n> I'm having trouble extracting the name `SomeAutoload` to display in the warning. But I'm not entirely sure if that _should_ be allowed. In any case, for right now it just defaults to \"The class is deprecated\".\r\n\r\nAutoloads are more a project setting than a class type but the parser shows the global name and path when there are errors. You can find the name like this `p_assignable->datatype_specifier->type_chain[0]->name`.\r\n\r\nBy the way, you can build with `warnings=extra werror=yes strict_checks=yes` to catch most of these CI issues locally.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2786847578/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814471499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104955#issuecomment-2814471499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104955","id":2814471499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6nwW1L","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-18T03:48:03Z","updated_at":"2025-04-18T03:48:03Z","body":"Thank you very much! 😄 I had that script for testing on my side, and realized it would make for a nice comprehensive unit test file.\r\n\r\nIt seems I have run into a bit of a pickle with the tests, though. It looks like at least the RenderingServer may not be constructed when running tests - trying to instantiate `AnimatedTexture` or `TileMap` in a test file causes the test to fail with a `SIGSEGV` error. When I add the following to the beginning of `AnimatedTexture`'s constructor, on the `master` branch:\r\n```cpp\r\nERR_FAIL_NULL_MSG(RS::get_singleton(), \"RenderingServer is null, so AnimatedTexture can't set itself up\");\r\n```\r\nIt prints out in the test results.\r\n\r\nI've changed it to use `VisualShaderNodeComment` for a native class and `AStarGrid2D.new().size` for a native property, which seem to partially work.\r\n`AnimatedTexture` is deprecated, of course, so I don't know how much effort should be put into updating it to work with tests. But this also happens with `Control.new()`, so *that* should probably be looked into further.\r\n\r\nBut tests on some other platforms appear to still be failing 🙁 \r\n```\r\nmodules\\gdscript\\tests\\gdscript_test_runner.cpp(217): ERROR: CHECK( result.passed ) is NOT correct!\r\n  values: CHECK( false )\r\n  logged: D:/a/godot/godot/modules/gdscript/tests/scripts/runtime/features/call_native_static_method_validated.gd\r\n          GDTEST_OK\r\nfalse\r\n166362874999 - Stray Node:  (Type: AnimationPlayer)\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2814471499/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847260137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104955#issuecomment-2847260137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104955","id":2847260137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ptb3p","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-02T13:49:55Z","updated_at":"2025-05-02T13:50:05Z","body":"> Re-run tests to generate new warning output\r\n> 　Add tests to detect use of deprecated identifiers?\r\n\r\nI assume these being unchecked is erroneous? The test you added seems sufficient, and if there were other changes needed, they'd be detected by GHA","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847260137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2847393125","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104955#issuecomment-2847393125","issue_url":"https://api.github.com