orge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-21T16:10:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-21T16:10:37Z","body":"Following discussions on the RocketChat, this PR has been updated to move the editor-reliant code into dedicated functions, and reduce the `TOOLS_ENABLED` blocks in the main analyzer to only a few short simple lines at a time. This way, it's much cleaner and easier to read!\r\n\r\nThe dedicated functions are public and static in `GDScriptAnalyzer` so they should be able to be called from other classes, in case we want to get deprecation status info there (such as in `gdscript_editor.cpp` for #100019 ). Notably though, I don't feel like there's anything that really *requires* these methods be a part of `GDScript` analyzer. So, if you feel there would be a different better class for them to live in, please let me know and I should be able to make that change fairly easily 🙂 ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5036318021/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]